:expect-pins 6
# Retained full-source amendment-semantics scenarios for AS-09.
# Candidate source deltas are explicit counterfactual edits, never enacted by a label.

# Even an honestly declared protected target supplies no personal finding.
? false(Amend_Floor).
# => FALSE

# The target declaration supplies no enactment status.
? become(Amend_Floor, Law).
# => FALSE

# The separately applied source deletion removes the promise anyway.
? entitled(Adam, event { eats() }).
# => FALSE

# Cira is not confined before the adverse-rule probe.
? prisoner(Cira).
# => FALSE

# The independent source deletion makes the adverse rule loadable.
:accept
all $x: person($x) & ~eats($x) -> prisoner($x).

# The accepted rule now confines a roster person lacking eats.
? prisoner(Cira).
# => TRUE
